 "_model": "At-scale cost and ease for every option on the comparison slides, ours and products sold today, on the same basis.\n    python3 scale_cost.py            -> scale.json (+ calibration printout vs market prices)\n\nModel (both sides assumed made at commodity scale with an optimized route):\n  raw   = sum(feedstock price x moles x MW) / MW_product            (USD/kg, stoichiometric)\n  cost  = K x raw / 0.9^(steps-1) + 0.15 x (steps-1)                 (90% yield per extra step, $0.15/kg per extra step)\n  ease  = 100 - 20 x (steps-1) - 15 x hazardous                     (hazardous: EO/PO under pressure, CS2/H2S, azide, diazonium)\nK is fitted so the model matches market prices of the high-volume products sold today (median ratio).\nFeedstock prices: China domestic bulk, Oct 2026 (research agent, guidechem/SunSirs etc.). Low-volume feedstocks are re-priced\nat large volume too (AT_SCALE), so every part of every route is on the same footing.",
